'''''Porphyra capensis''''' is a species of [[red algae]] in the family of [[Bangiaceae]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.algaebase.org/search/species/detail/?species_id=1698|title=Porphyra capensis Kützing 1843 |author=Guiry M.D. |publisher=AlgaeBase |accessdate=11 July 2026}}</ref> Its name stems from it being first described from a sample taken from the [[Cape of Good Hope]].<ref>{{cite thesis |last1=Yalo |first1=Masande Nicholas |title=An investigation of the natural products composition of Porphyra capensis (a red seaweed) |date=2017 |hdl=10566/14394 }}{{pn|date=July 2026}}</ref> In addition to the coasts of South Africa, it has also been observed growing along the coasts of [[Namibia]].<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Zhang |first1=Quanbin |last2=Qi |first2=Huimin |last3=Zhao |first3=Tingting |last4=Deslandes |first4=Eric |last5=Ismaeli |first5=Ninasayaeli Mbise |last6=Molloy |first6=F. |last7=Critchley |first7=Alan T. |title=Chemical characteristics of a polysaccharide from Porphyra capensis (Rhodophyta) |journal=Carbohydrate Research |date=October 2005 |volume=340 |issue=15 |pages=2447–2450 |doi=10.1016/j.carres.2005.08.009 |pmid=16150429 }}</ref>

